Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 22:27:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(sim): custom-trigger rng routing by KIND-AWARE
 signature inspection, replacing the broad per-draw TypeError fallback. The
 RNG-unification commit supported old-style triggers (simulate_trigger(pars)
 -- a legacy THIRD-PARTY shape: both in-repo trigger classes, including
 Temporal_Power_Law, were made new-style in that same commit) via try:
 trig.simulate_trigger(par, rng=rng) / except TypeError:
 trig.simulate_trigger(par), executed INSIDE the cascade loop on every draw.
 Audit finding, RED-verified at the pre-fix tip: the catch misclassifies ANY
 TypeError raised inside a NEW-style trigger as an old signature and silently
 re-executes it without rng -- masked user bug, quietly abandoned
 reproducibility, side effects run twice; Generator/RandomState API mismatches
 make this realistic (Generator has no .randn, RandomState no .integers).
 Observed: a new-style trigger raising TypeError on its Generator path was
 swallowed and _sim_offspring completed with 9 rows drawn off the Generator.
 Fix: utils.accepts_rng_kwarg inspects the bound simulate_trigger signature
 ONCE per _sim_offspring call. Classification is KIND-aware per review, not
 name-only: 'rng' counts only where rng=... is a valid call form
 (POSITIONAL_OR_KEYWORD or KEYWORD_ONLY), plus **kwargs; a POSITIONAL_ONLY rng
 (def f(pars, rng, /)) and a VAR_POSITIONAL *rng classify OLD-style -- the
 withdrawn name-only draft classified the positional-only case new-style, and
 the rng= call it would then make raises TypeError('got some positional-only
 arguments passed as keyword'), turning a WORKING legacy trigger into a crash
 (observed; review-caught). Uninspectable C callables fall back to the legacy
 form. RNG streams unchanged for all in-repo triggers (new-style: same rng=rng
 call as before). New tests/test_trigger_compat.py (5): detector
 classification pinning BOTH in-repo trigger classes as new-style (a detector
 that dropped Temporal_Power_Law from the Generator stream would silently
 break reproducibility) plus the kind edge cases; the mask regression
 (internal TypeError must surface; RED pre-fix); legacy-shape support under
 Generator-driven simulation; the positional-only trigger running live through
 _sim_offspring via the legacy call form; **kwargs triggers receiving the
 caller's Generator. Verified: 57/57; fixed-seed cox_hawkes simulate
 byte-identical across the commit; all four value+gradient pin configs
 bit-identical; ruff clean on bstpp/.

